{"arrivo":"en","origine":"dz","origine_nome":"Dzongkha","n":21,"parole":[{"parola":"ara","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":2,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"A traditional alcoholic beverage consumed in Bhutan, made from rice, maize, millet, or wheat, either fermented or disti…","termine_origine":"ཨ་རག་","catena":[{"codice":"dz","nome":"Dzongkha","termine":"ཨ་རག་","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"ar","nome":"Arabic","termine":"عرق","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ar","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowing from Dzongkha ཨ་རག་ (a rag), ultimately from Arabic عرق (ʕaraq). Doublet of arak."},{"parola":"chetrum","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"A subdivision of currency, equal to one hundredth of a Bhutanese ngultrum","termine_origine":"ཕྱེད་ཏམ","catena":[{"codice":"dz","nome":"Dzongkha","termine":"ཕྱེད་ཏམ","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"dz","ambiti":["finanza"],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Dzongkha ཕྱེད་ཏམ (phyed tam)."},{"parola":"chilip","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"A foreigner, especially a Westerner; someone from outside Bhutan or the broader Tibetan cultural sphere.","termine_origine":"ཕྱི་གླིང་པ","catena":[{"codice":"dz","nome":"Dzongkha","termine":"ཕྱི་གླིང་པ","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"dz","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Dzongkha ཕྱི་གླིང་པ (phyi gling pa, literally “person from the outer continent”). A common folk etymology links it to grey hair, referring to the lighter hair color of many Westerners."},{"parola":"chiwog","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"An administrative division in Bhutan, formerly comprising municipalities below the level of gewog.","termine_origine":"སྤྱི་འོག","catena":[{"codice":"dz","nome":"Dzongkha","termine":"སྤྱི་འོག","categoria":"prestito"}],"lontana":"dz","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Borrowed from Dzongkha སྤྱི་འོག (spyi 'og)."